{
 "name": "plastic-sulfur-basic",
 "description": "Early oil: plastic bars and sulfur from crude oil with BASIC oil processing (it can't deadlock: the refineries make only petroleum). 3 oil refineries on basic-oil-processing (5 s: 100 crude -> 45 petroleum, so 20 crude -> 9 petroleum per s each) feed two separate petroleum pipes: 2 refineries (18 petroleum/s) -> 1 chemical plant on plastic-bar (1 s: 20 petroleum + 1 coal -> 2 plastic; runs at 90%), 1 refinery (9/s) -> 1 chemical plant on sulfur (1 s: 30 petroleum + 30 water -> 2 sulfur; runs at 30%). Kept separate on purpose: on one shared pipe the game splits petroleum about evenly between the plants (tested: 1.2 plastic + 1.0 sulfur per s). Tested at all four rotations: 1.8 plastic bars/s (108/min) and 0.6 sulfur/s (36/min). That covers one advanced-circuit-block (1.5 plastic/s) + one chemical-science-block (0.25 sulfur/s), i.e. 30 chemical science/min, with plastic and sulfur to spare. Either output may back up without stopping the other (tested: plastic not taken, sulfur still 0.6/s; sulfur not taken, plastic still 1.8/s). Inputs: crude oil 60/s and water 9/s (pipes), coal 0.9/s (belt, either lane). Outputs: plastic and sulfur on separate belts. Never feed other fluids into its pipes. Power about 1.8 MW peak (3 x 420 kW + 2 x 210 kW + 3 fast inserters).",
